    - pick duplication axis (horizontal or vertical) randomly
    - pick 3-4 distinct colors from 1-9
    - fill tile randomly with chosen colors ensuring every color appears at least once
    - reject if tile has equal halves along any axis (both H and V); retry fill if so
    - construct input by concatenating tile with itself along chosen axis
    - verify exactly one split axis works on the resulting input (should hold by construction)
```
